# Agent Workflow

Source: `@AGENT.md`.

## States

`idle → planning → awaiting_approval → executing → verifying → complete`

- Do not skip `planning` for multi-file or risky changes.
- Mutations require explicit user approval when scope is ambiguous or destructive.
- Crash resume: check `sessions/` and `@MEMORY.md` checkpoint protocol.

## Agent types (Cursor mapping)

| Type | Cursor surface | Constraints |
|------|----------------|-------------|
| explore | Ask / read-only chat | No edits |
| plan | Plan mode | No implementation |
| implement | Agent / Composer | Full tools per safety tiers |
| verify | Agent with test focus | No feature edits; run checks |
| guide | Chat | Explain only |

## Composer multi-file

1. List target files/globs before editing.
2. Edit related layers together (route + service + test + types).
3. End with verification checklist tied to spec scenarios.

## Parallel work

- Use explore subtasks for read-only investigation across large trees.
- Keep one Composer thread authoritative for writes to avoid conflicts.
